course: dictionary
lesson: 14486
title: Patriarch: the head of a family
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A patriarch is a man who leads a family or tribe, usually the oldest man. The word is long, so read the words around it to find its meaning. «Grandad is the patriarch of our family, and everyone asks his advice.»
explain: The clues are everyone asks his advice. People ask a leader for advice, so patriarch must mean the head of the family. Check it by putting your meaning in the sentence: «Grandad is the head of our family, and everyone asks his advice.» It still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: The word can also be used in Bible stories and in church. «In the Bible, Abraham, Isaac and Jacob are called patriarchs.» Here it names the great early fathers of the people of Israel. In some churches, a patriarch is a bishop of the highest rank.
fact: A patriarch is the head of a family or tribe, often the oldest man.
fact: «Patriarch» comes from a Greek word meaning father and ruler of a family.
fact: In the Bible, the patriarchs are Abraham, Isaac and Jacob, whose stories are in the book of Genesis.
fact: In some churches, such as the Orthodox Churches, a patriarch is a bishop of the highest rank.
fact: A woman who leads a family is sometimes called a matriarch, the female word for the same idea.
exercise: «The patriarch of the family made the big decisions.» What does patriarch mean? | A small child who plays in the garden | A cook in a busy kitchen | *The head of a family, often the oldest | A bird that sings at dawn
exercise: In the Bible, who are the patriarchs? | Adam, Eve and Cain | Noah, Moses and Ruth | *Abraham, Isaac and Jacob
exercise: What clue in «Grandad is the patriarch of our family, and everyone asks his advice» shows he is the leader? | Our family | The word Grandad | Is | *Everyone asks his advice
test: «The old patriarch sat at the head of the long table.» What is a patriarch? | A kind of table | *The head of a family, often the oldest | A small boat | A type of bread
test: In some churches, what is a patriarch? | A king who lives in a castle | A singer in a choir | *A bishop of the highest rank in some churches | A teacher at a school
exam: Which word means a woman who leads a family? | Patriarch | Monk | Priest | *Matriarch
